 but we just released a small update to adjust normal difficulty. Check it out here: https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/2956680/view/533253197651772627", "app_release_date": "1769006794", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 28, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "222154921", "author": {"steamid": "76561198179354413", "personaname": "Pee-Air de Toebertin", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198179354413/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 23, "playtime_forever": 1873, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 419, "last_played": 1787972361, "avatar": "4b44bfaed569cb962dbf36098cc96a322331740e"}, "language": "english", "review": "Vibe-- I think this game has a lot of character, I think it is an interesting iteration on the rouge-like/rouge-lite formula. Love that you can play with up to 8 friends, that's something that I haven't experienced in a rogue-like game before. I like the art direction, there are visual puns (Lawrence fish-bird cracked me up a lot when I took a closer look at his character model), the ren-fair type aesthetic I enjoy a lot, kind of feels like a bunch of people LARPing a DND campaign and I think that's really fun. I really like the tongue-in-cheek humor. Reminds me of playing DND with friends and making out-of-setting jokes or references, I think the art direction in this game captures that feeling really well.\n\nGameplay positives -- abilities are cool, classes feel distinct from one another, there are opportunities to collaborate beyond combat. My favorite emergent gameplay so far has been stumbling on a shop, finding an upgrade that really suits one member of the team, and pooling money for that person to get the thing that helps their build. Each stage is fun to unlock and play for the first time, they're distinct aesthetically and in terms of gameplay. Challenge is something I would like to see sustained, I really enjoyed the feeling of beating the second stage boss for the first time after figuring out a good team composition to tackle that boss fight.\n\nConstructive criticism -- some classes feel much stronger than others (mage feels really strong compared to rogue and barbarian). Difficulty spikes between levels feel unfair, meaning you have a tiered loot system that is RNG (either you get your class's current loot tier weapon(s) for the current stage or you don't based on drop chance that the player can't meaningfully control). Having an underpowered weapon for the level you're on feels really bad, I think minimizing that through a system that the player can influence/control besides juice upgrades that make weapon spawn sprites free would be nice. I think it would feel more fair if there was a telegraphed activity to complete per level that guaranteed an appropriate loot tier weapon for your class at the start of the next level (i.e. kill this thing and some vendor will have a weapon of the appropriate loot level for the next stage that you can buy in the hub) -- that would give an interesting choice of what to do with your gold as well, spend it on chests in level or save it for vendors at the end of the stage.\n\nClosing thoughts -- I keep coming back so I know it has some of that indie game magic. I think with some fine-tuning this will make a very memorable and long-lasting game.", "timestamp_created": 1774935083, "timestamp_updated": 1774935210, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.52173912525177002", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1769006794", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "222152092", "author": {"steamid": "76561198169098232", "personaname": "i frekd ya mum", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198169098232/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 3, "playtime_forever": 283, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 283, "last_played": 1774930846, "avatar": "370ee14383528f44cf0f921bbdc1fb6a164165dc"}, "language": "english", "review": "The scaling on this game is terrible", "timestamp_created": 1774930899, "timestamp_updated": 1774930899, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 9, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.584967613220214844", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "timestamp_dev_responded": 1774986998, "developer_response": "Thanks for the review and heard on the feedback. We have more difficulty scaling plans in our next big update, but we just released a small update to adjust normal difficulty. Check it out here: https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/2956680/view/533253197651772627", "app_release_date": "1769006794", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "222151089", "author": {"steamid": "76561198878983100", "personaname": "MarkDaddy", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198878983100/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 1005, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 981, "last_played": 1775069518, "avatar": "950f9f3147d4c8530a5072825d01c34ee3f1afa1"}, "language": "english", "review": "8/10", "timestamp_created": 1774929503, "timestamp_updated": 1774929503, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1769006794", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "222150541", "author": {"steamid": "76561198043914625", "personaname": "BIG_Will777", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/BIG_will777/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 39, "playtime_forever": 180, "playtime_last